everal bounds on the\n\ndegree of reconstructible graphs have been shown (cf. [4, 5, 6, 7, 13]). A\n\nmajor result in this area has been obtained by Krasikov and Roditty [13,\n\nRemark 2]. They proved an analogue of Kelly’s Lemma to reconstruct the\n\nnumber of subgraphs in a graph. To state the result, some more notation is\n\nneeded. Given graphs G and H, let X s(G→H) denote the number of sets\n\nU⊂V(G), |U|=s, such that G U is isomorphic to H. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSwitching reconstruction problems for signed graphs (https://repositorio.ufmg.br/items/96f8e1ec-7f89-46a5-8d7c-f6f58f9d5b8f)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.7 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; The Reconstruction Conjecture asserts that every finite simple graph, with at least three vertices, is determined, up to isomorphism, by its collection of unlabelled vertex-deleted subgraphs. ... We call the problem the sign switching reconstruction problem.\n\n# Switching reconstruction problems for signed graphs\n\nCarregando...\n\n## Arquivos\n\nTese_doutorado__Amanda_-2.pdf (1.25 MB)\n\n## Data\n\n2024-03-01\n\n## Autor(es)\n\nAmanda Caroline Silva\n\n## Editor\n\nUniversidade Federal de Minas Gerais\n\n## Tipo\n\nTese de doutorado\n\n## Título alternativo\n\nProblemas de reconstrução de grafos por troca de sinal\n\n## Primeiro orientador\n\nBhalchandra Digambar Thatte\n\n## Membros da banca\n\nCsaba Schneider\nFábio Happ Botler\nMonique Müller Lopes Rocha\nViktor Bekkert\n\n## Resumo\n\nLet G be a simple graph. Consider the multiset of all unlabelled graphs obtained by deleting a vertex v of G together with all the edges incident with v. This multiset is called the collection of vertex-deleted subgraphs of G. The Reconstruction Conjecture asserts that every finite simple graph, with at least three vertices, is determined, up to isomorphism, by its collection of unlabelled vertex-deleted subgraphs. This conjecture was first formulated in 1941, by Kelly and Ulam. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpectra of graphs Andries E. Brouwer Willem H. Haemers (https://studylib.net/doc/10499363/spectra-of-graphs-andries-e.-brouwer-willem-h.-haemers)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago;     the same degree are related by Seidel switching, the switch is also a case of GM ...     so that any counterexample to the reconstruction conjecture must be a pair of\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ngraph theory - Reconstruction conjecture: Can other decks do the job? - MathOverflow (https://mathoverflow.net/questions/25215/reconstruction-conjecture-can-other-decks-do-the-job)\nciteturn0search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.5 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; So, any counterexample to one of the candidates above would be very welcome. ... There is also the vertex-switching reconstruction conjecture and the $k$-reconstruction conjecture (see Bondy's Graph Reconstructor's Manual for definitions).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReconstruction from Vertex-Switching (https://studylib.net/doc/8127868/reconstruction-from-vertex-switching)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 41.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; # Reconstruction from Vertex-Switching ... 15.17a] on the edge-reconstruction conjecture.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnlocking the Reconstruction Conjecture: A Dual Structure–Transformation Framework Between Vertex Decks, Overlapping Shadows, and Global Graph Coherence | Continuous Learning & Development (https://ppalme.wordpress.com/2026/09/12/unlocking-the-reconstruction-conjecture-a-dual-structure-transformation-framework-between-vertex-decks-overlapping-shadows-and-global-graph-coherence/)\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; This is an 